<title>LUXEMBOURG: Luxembourg allows DuPont to use CFC 11.</title>
<headline>Luxembourg allows DuPont to use CFC 11.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Luxembourg environment ministry said on Thursday it was allowing DuPont de Nemours to use the refrigerant CFC (chloroflourocarbon) 11 in its Luxembourg production plant until December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The ministry said the decision was in line with the so-called Montreal Protocol which aims to regulate and ban the use of substances which are damaging to the ozone layer.</p>
<p>DuPont is investing 3.5 billion Luxembourg francs in a new production unit which will use a refrigerating agent which will have no impact on the ozone layer.</p>
